<title>Japan: Nippon Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Nippon Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Trust Bank Ltd has disclosed</p>
<p>its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Mar 97     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans		4.6		3.5</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  14.5	     13.4</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	   23.8	     25.1</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    42.9	     42.0</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more.</p>
</text>
